    "body": "## What\n\nRoadmap M2.3, M2.4, M2.10: chirpo can log in to GitHub.\n\n- **GitHub App login** (`adapters/codehost/github/auth.py`, githubkit): signs a JWT with the App key, looks up the installation for a repo (cached per repo), and uses an installation token **scoped to that one repo**. githubkit caches and renews the tokens.\n- **Dev token fallback**: `CHIRPO_GITHUB_DEV_TOKEN` when no App is configured; still refused in production.\n- **Error translation** (`errors.py`): githubkit errors become core `CodeHost*` errors, including failures wrapped inside the auth flow; a 401 says the credentials were rejected.\n- **Retry policy**: server errors retried twice for reads only (a failed write may still have happened, so retrying could duplicate an issue); rate limits retried once only when the wait is \u2264 5 s, otherwise raised so a worker never sleeps for minutes.\n- **`chirpo github whoami [owner/repo]`**: shows the identity, whether the repo is reachable, and the App's permissions.\n- **Settings**: an App ID without a key path is rejected.\n- **Docker**: `./secrets` mounted read-only at `/run/secrets/chirpo`, container key path set by Compose. The Dockerfile keeps uv downloads in a build cache and downloads less in parallel, so builds survive slow networks.\n- **Logging**: PEM private keys inside log text are redacted.\n- **Guide**: `docs/github-app.md` (create, install, configure, check), linked from the README.\n\nReviewed with the ECC python and security reviewers; findings fixed.\n\n## How to test\n\n```bash\ncd backend\nuv run pytest tests/integration/test_github_auth.py tests/unit -q\nuv run chirpo github whoami owner/repo     # needs a configured App (docs/github-app.md)\ndocker compose run --rm --no-deps api chirpo github whoami owner/repo\n```\n\nChecked live against a private sandbox repo, on the host and in Docker.\n",
